// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission1Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P303040762" "Bravo for the Shadow Shard"
// DetailString :
"P3154872956" "Information you'd already captured from the Nemesis Army indicate that the heroes and the Nemesis Army seemed to be fighting in a strange pocket dimension called the Shadow Shard. You struck a Portal Corp Facility to find some confirmation, and forced one of their scientists to give you the information you needed."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission2Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P4143267298" "Information you'd already captured from the Nemesis Army indicate that the heroes and the Nemesis Army seemed to be fighting in a strange pocket dimension called the Shadow Shard. You struck a Portal Corp Facility to find some confirmation, and forced one of their scientists to give you the information you needed. <br><br>Using the information you stole, you used Naylor's portal to cross over into a strange alternate dimension at a base called 'Mole Point Bravo'. You defeated the defenders and kidnapped some of the natives for information."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SL7_Naylor_MiniArc1A_SouvenirClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P3678917354" "Last Stand on Mole Point Bravo"
// tDetailString :
"P3970180943" "Information you'd already captured from the Nemesis Army indicate that the heroes and the Nemesis Army seemed to be fighting in a strange pocket dimension called the Shadow Shard. You struck a Portal Corp Facility to find some confirmation, and forced one of their scientists to give you the information you needed. <br><br>Using the information you stole, you used Naylor's portal to cross over into a strange alternate dimension at a base called 'Mole Point Bravo'. You defeated the defenders and kidnapped some of the natives for information. <br><br>Shortly after you left, things started to go horribly wrong on Mole Point Bravo. You went to fend off a Longbow Counter-attack and found the base was also under attack by the strange creatures called the 'Rularuu'. You took a final job to get the base commander out of danger so he could evacuate the place, leaving what's left of Mole Point Bravo to the heroes and the monsters of the Shadow Shard."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SL7_Naylor_MiniArc1B_SouvenirClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P1879614032" "The Fall of Mole Point Bravo"
// tDetailString :
"P2767066427" "Information you'd already captured from the Nemesis Army indicate that the heroes and the Nemesis Army seemed to be fighting in a strange pocket dimension called the Shadow Shard. You struck a Portal Corp Facility to find some confirmation, and forced one of their scientists to give you the information you needed. <br><br>Using the information you stole, you used Naylor's portal to cross over into a strange alternate dimension at a base called 'Mole Point Bravo'. You defeated the defenders and kidnapped some of the natives for information. <br><br>Shortly after you left, things started to go horribly wrong on Mole Point Bravo. You went to fend off a Longbow Counter-attack and found the base was also under attack by the strange creatures called the 'Rularuu'. You took a final job to get the base commander out of danger so he could evacuate the place, but the fool never made it back. Arachnos lost a lot of people, and Mole Point Bravo is now left for the strange monsters of the Shadow Shard."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1469239378" "'Ey {VillainName}, you remember that information ya' gaffed from tha Nemesis Army for me a bit back? <br>Well, I was goin' through it, lookin' for more stable dimensions, when I noticed there was this one spot they mentioned the 'eeroes were also explorin'. So I talked ta some buddies o' mine in intel, an' they told me that captured Nemesis Army soldiers 'ave been talkin' 'bout somethin' called tha 'Shadow Shard', another dimension where they're fightin' the 'eeroes an' stuff. I think it's the same place. This could be worth checkin' out, but we'd need to know it's tha same place. Ta do that, <A HREF={ACCEPT}>we need coordinates from tha 'eeroes. An' I know just 'ow ta get them.</A> <br>I will warn ya, though, if ya start this, your in it, right? So C'mon, it should be fun, eh?"
// AcceptString :
"P3262789580" "Get coordinates for the 'Shadow Shard' from Portal Corp"
// SendOffString :
"P1125212695" "Yer gonna love this. 'Ere's tha plan: I set me portal 'ere ta intercept tha next time tha 'eeroes try to send somethin' over ta this Shadow Shard. After the transit's done, it's kept locked on their portal, and now I can force the other end a' their portal back open. So all you got to do is gear up, go through, an' force one a' their portal techs to get the data from their computers. If it matches, we're in luck."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P504215833" "Force Scientist to get data"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P491615900" "Force their chief scientist ta get the information for ya. That should do tha trick."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P422224205" "You hear a voice echo from the other side of the portal: 'Huh. It really worked!'"

